From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:42:26 -0700
Subject: mfd: macsmc: count a port's dark wake on every board with a sleep
 policy

apple_smc_prepare_guard() waits for a command in flight only when
dark_wakes is set, and apple_smc_dark_wake() returns for every board but
the J714s before it counts a wake that apple_sleep_port_wake() already
made dark. On the other boards with a sleep policy (the J716c) the guard
at .suspend after a port's wake with the lid closed is then a single
trylock: if a command of the wake is still running, .suspend returns
-EBUSY and the dark wake ends in a full one.

Count the wake first, then keep the J714s's own rule to the J714s. The
comment on the wait no longer names the J714s.

A board without a sleep policy (the J813) does not get here and is not
changed.

Fixes: 18b493373c7c ("mfd: macsmc: J714s: keep the port and radio dark wakes to the J714s")
Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
---
 drivers/mfd/macsmc.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c b/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
index 9fee7a0c5d0..dad38e98e24 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/macsmc.c
@@ -1070,14 +1070,14 @@ static void apple_smc_dark_wake(struct apple_smc *smc)
 	const char *why = is_radio ? "wifibt" : "USB-C_plug";
 	s64 asleep_ms;
 
-	/* The J714s's rule alone: other boards with a sleep policy keep these wakes full. */
-	if (smc->wake_reasons != apple_smc_j714s_wake_reasons)
-		return;
 	/* Already dark (a port's wake with the lid closed): counted, so the re-entry waits as after ours. */
 	if (pm_dark_wake()) {
 		smc->dark_wakes++;
 		return;
 	}
+	/* The J714s's rule alone: other boards with a sleep policy keep these wakes full. */
+	if (smc->wake_reasons != apple_smc_j714s_wake_reasons)
+		return;
 	if (!is_radio && (port < 0 || smc->wake_record != BIT_ULL(port)))
 		return;
 	asleep_ms = ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get_boottime(), smc->sleep_entry_boot) -
@@ -1618,7 +1618,7 @@ static int apple_smc_prepare_policy(struct apple_smc *smc)
 
 /*
  * The saved-context guard, under the command mutex, without waiting for it: a sleep a user asks
- * for doesn't wait on a stuck command. The re-entry right after a J714s dark wake does, for at
+ * for doesn't wait on a stuck command. The re-entry right after a counted dark wake does, for at
  * most SMC_DARK_REENTRY_MS: the notification of the event that woke it is still being handled
  * then, its ordinary command in flight, and refusing ended every dark wake in a full one.
  */
